# @@GARDEN@@ — the garden's own rows

The rows this garden adds to the law, under the keys MODEL.md names: `kinds`, `levels`, `namespaces`, `flows`,
`flow_sources`, `standing`, `verbs`, `units`, `tables` (rows added to a table the verbs name) and `exclusive`. A row
never takes a name the law has, and every row is used by a bean or says why it is vacant (`vacant: <why>`): add it
with the first bean that uses it. This file is law, so its entry says RULE-CHANGE. A row that proves general is
proposed to the standard.
